<div type="letter">
<div type="mainBody">
<p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: The <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">edition</rs> at 150 francs</seg> is now out of print. If any article appears in the <hi rend="underline">Times</hi> <hi rend="underline">Literary</hi> <hi rend="underline">Supplement</hi> tomorrow (Thursday) will you please send me three copies?</p>
<closer>	
<salute>With kind regards</salute>
                                                       	<salute>sincerely yours</salute>
        	                                                       	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
<dateline>
                            <date when="1922-03-15">15/III/922</date>
                        </dateline>
</closer>
</div>
</div>



<div type="notes">

<note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Of the first 1,000 copies of the first printing of <hi rend="italic">Ulysses</hi>, 100 were printed on Dutch handmade paper, signed by JJ, and sold for 350 francs. Another 150 were printed on <hi rend="italic">vergé d’Arches</hi> and sold for 250 francs. The remaining 750 copies were printed on handmade paper and sold for 150 francs. For more details on the first printing of <hi rend="italic">Ulysses</hi> see notes for <rs type="letter" key="L_68800">JJ to Pound, 11 October 1921</rs> and <rs type="letter" key="L_68851">JJ to Pound, 2 February 1922</rs>.</note>
                    
</div>








